  message: "SEQUENCING AGAINST THE OWNER'S ARC, decided 2026-08-26 at the owner's request.\nThe arc is:\n\n    INV-pusin -> WI-lutuh + INV-zimud -> INV-vivok -> WI-fosir / INV-hosul -> P7\n\nTHIS ITEM IS NOT A NEW ARC STAGE. It is a required COMPONENT of stage 2.\n`module_completeness: complete` asserts that EVERY I/O primitive a module\nexposes is catalogued. A clock is now I/O (WI-pavob, \"yes in\"), so any module\nexposing a clock cannot be declared complete until its clock rows exist. For\nrust that work already sits inside WI-pavob and is ruled. For the other fourteen\nlanguages it gets absorbed into each language's WI-lutuh decomposition as that\ndecomposition happens. This item exists so no language is silently skipped, NOT\nso it can be scheduled on its own.\n\nTHE REAL CONSTRAINT IS A MEASUREMENT CONFOUND, and it is the actionable half.\nThe arc is FALSE-INCONCLUSIVE work: it makes withheld verdicts resolve. This\nitem points the OPPOSITE way -- it makes host_info_read fire near-universally\nand therefore produces MORE VIOLATED verdicts. A repository that should have\nmoved inconclusive -> clean under an arc fix may instead move\ninconclusive -> VIOLATED, so the arc's payoff would read as smaller than it is,\nand nobody could tell whether a fix underperformed or the clock rows ate the\nimprovement.\n\n  RULE: land this BEFORE the arc's baseline measurements are taken, or AFTER\n  they are complete. NEVER between. Same discipline as A/B-ing the tool rather\n  than the history.\n\nDOWNSTREAM EFFECT ON WI-fosir, recorded there as well. This item ADDS ROWS, so\nmore calls classify, so the uncatalogued-module list gets SHORTER. WI-fosir is\nthe 5-name cap on that same list, so measuring WI-fosir before this lands would\ncalibrate a truncation against a denominator about to shrink -- the identical\ninteraction INV-pusin already had with it."  # 4132
